-- title:
--   Coordinate ring of the n-torsion is B[[X₁,X₂]]/(φ₁,φ₂)
-- statement:
--   Let $B$ be a noetherian commutative ring, $A$ a scheme, $f : A \to \operatorname{Spec} B$, and $L$ a relative group law on $f$, i.e. a group structure on the sections $\{\varphi : T \to A \mid \varphi \circ f = t\}$ for each $t : T \to \operatorname{Spec} B$, natural in $T$. Let $F$ be a $2$-dimensional formal group law over $B$ and $\theta$ a family assigning to each $B$-algebra $B'$ and each $s \in (B')^2$ a section of $f$ over $\operatorname{Spec} B'$, such that `L.IsFormalCoordinates F θ` holds: $\theta$ is compatible with $B$-algebra maps on nilpotent tuples, and for every ideal $J$ of a $B$-algebra $B'$ with $J^{k+1} = 0$, $\theta$ restricts to a bijection from $J$-tuples onto the points that become the unit modulo $J$, carrying the truncated formal multiplication `F.nilMul` to the group law. Let $\varphi = (\varphi_1,\varphi_2)$ be power series in two variables over $B$ with zero constant terms such that, for every $B$-algebra $B'$, ideal $J$ with $J^{k+1} = 0$ and $s$ with entries in $J$, one has $\theta_{B'}(\varphi_i(s)) = n \cdot \theta_{B'}(s)$, where $\varphi_i(s)$ is the evaluation [`MvFormalGroup.nilEval k`](def/AlgebraicGeometry_FormalGroupAlongSection.html#L15) of $\varphi_i$ at $s$ and $n \cdot$ is the $n$-fold iterate `L.nsmul` of the group law. Assume further that every $n$-torsion section over every $B$-algebra $B'$ is infinitesimal: it becomes the unit modulo some nilpotent ideal $J$ of $B'$. Finally let $R$ be a $B$-algebra and $e$ an isomorphism of $\operatorname{Spec} R$ with `L.schemeKer n`, the pullback of the $n$-multiplication endomorphism `L.schemeNsmul n` of $A$ along the unit section, such that $e$ followed by the structure map `L.schemeKerStr n` is $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $B \to R$. Then there exist an ideal $J \subseteq R$, an integer $\nu \ge 1$ with $J^{\nu+1} = 0$, and $s_0 \in R^2$ with entries in $J$, such that $\theta_R(s_0)$ is the universal $n$-torsion point $e$ followed by `pullback.fst`, together with a $B$-algebra isomorphism $E : B[[X_1,X_2]]/(\varphi_1,\varphi_2) \xrightarrow{\sim} R$ given on every class by $E(\bar G) =$ [`MvFormalGroup.nilEval ν G s₀`](def/AlgebraicGeometry_FormalGroupAlongSection.html#L15), the evaluation at $s_0$ of the truncation of $G$ in degrees $\le \nu$ in each variable.
--
--   This identifies the affine algebra of the kernel of multiplication by $n$ on a group scheme with formal coordinates, under the hypothesis that all $n$-torsion points are infinitesimal, with the quotient of the two-variable power series ring by the ideal generated by the series representing multiplication by $n$; the isomorphism is pinned by sending $\bar G$ to $G(s_0)$ for the coordinates $s_0$ of the universal torsion point. It is used in the comparison of the algebra of $p$-torsion of a fake elliptic curve at a ramified place with the truncated special formal module, through [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.exists_isFormalModuleVia_algEquiv_kerAlgebra_forall_apply_eq_nilEval_of_ramified`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.exists_isFormalModuleVia_algEquiv_kerAlgebra_forall_apply_eq_nilEval_of_ramified).
